L000700	\section{Numerical evaluation of the compressible and incompressible energy spectra}
L000701	Given the weighted superfluid velocity $\boldsymbol{u}$, we outline the procedure to extract its irrotational and solenoidal components, $\boldsymbol{u}_{c}$ and $\boldsymbol{u}_{i}$, respectively.
L000702	
L000703	Using the Green's function \cite{Watanabe2013}, any
L000704	two-dimensional vector field $\boldsymbol{V} \left( \boldsymbol{r}\right)$ can be expressed as
L000705	\begin{equation}\label{vector_integral_identity}
L000706	\boldsymbol{V} \left( \boldsymbol{r}\right)
L000707	=
L000708	\int
L000709	\boldsymbol{V} \left( \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime}\right)
L000710	\delta \left( \boldsymbol{r} - \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime} \right)
L000711	\, d^2 \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime}
L000712	=
L000713	\nabla^2
L000714	\left\lbrack
L000715	\frac{1}{2 \pi}
L000716	\int
L000717	\boldsymbol{V} \left( \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime}\right)
L000718	\ln \left( \frac{\left\vert \boldsymbol{r} - \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime} \right\vert}{l} \right)
L000719	\,
L000720	d^2 \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime}
L000721	\right\rbrack
L000722	,
L000723	\end{equation}
L000724	where $\delta \left( \boldsymbol{r} \right)$ is the two-dimensional Dirac delta function
L000725	and $l$ is a constant with units of length.
L000726	Applying Eq. (\ref{vector_integral_identity}) to $\boldsymbol{u}(\boldsymbol{r})$ yields $\boldsymbol{u}(\boldsymbol{r})=\nabla^{2}\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{r})$, where $
L000727	\boldsymbol{b} \left( \boldsymbol{r}\right)
L000728	\coloneqq
L000729	\left( 1 / 2 \pi \right)
L000730	\int
L000731	\boldsymbol{u} \left( \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime} \right)
L000732	\ln \left( \left\vert \boldsymbol{r} - \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime} \right\vert / l \right)
L000733	\, d^2 \boldsymbol{r}^{\prime}
L000734	$.
L000735	Using the vector identity $\nabla \times \left( \nabla \times \boldsymbol{A} \right) = \nabla \left( \nabla \cdot \boldsymbol{A} \right) - \nabla^2 \boldsymbol{A}$, we can thus decompose $\boldsymbol{u}$ into:
L000736	\begin{equation}
L000737	\boldsymbol{u}_{c} \left( \boldsymbol{r}, t \right)
L000738	=
L000739	\nabla
L000740	\left\lbrack
L000741	\nabla
L000742	\cdot
L000743	\boldsymbol{b} \left( \boldsymbol{r}, t \right)
L000744	\right\rbrack
L000745	, \quad
L000746	\boldsymbol{u}_{i} \left( \boldsymbol{r}, t \right)
